    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d412">

                <pb facs="0550" n="470" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg470"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Storer.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-06-04"><hi rendition="#italic">June 4,
                        1901.</hi></date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 337.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    No. 474, of the 21st ultimo, in which, referring to Department’s No. 320, of
                    April 8 last, you state that you have reached the conclusion that Mr. Benito
                    Llaveria Pascual was by Spanish law domiciled in Barcelona at the time of his
                    enrollment for the army in 1898; that he was of proper age to be enrolled, and
                    that his failure to present himself for such purpose places him entirely under
                    the penal sections cited by the commission.</p>
                <p>You add that you have advised the United States consul-general at Barcelona of
                    your conclusions.</p>
                <p>In reply I have to say that the Department approves your action.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
